From 041b7f3c8a45db77a2a4ff325f1be8e87de09572 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 2 Aug 2026 18:16:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] feat(printing): add a minimal IPP client

Speaks just enough IPP (RFC 8011) to submit a document, read a job's state,
query a printer and list a CUPS server's queues.

Deliberately not pycups: that is a C extension against libcups and would add
libcups2-dev plus a compile step to the Docker build for everyone, including
users who never print from the server. IPP is a binary payload over HTTP POST,
so this encodes it directly using httpx, which is already a dependency. No new
dependency, no new system package.
